.TH WORMS 6.SH NAMEworms \- worms crawl the screen.SH SYNOPSIS\fBworms\fR[\-field] [\-length n] [\-number n] [\-trail].SH DESCRIPTIONWorms wander the screen at random, each drawn in a letter of its own,turning away from the edges, until control-C stops them.  A screen toy,by Eric P. Scott of Caltech, 1980.  It draws through TERMCAP..SH OPTIONS.TP 12\fB\-number\fI n\fRhow many worms..TP 12\fB\-length\fI n\fRhow long each one is..TP 12\fB\-trail\fReach worm leaves a trail behind it..TP 12\fB\-field\fRfill the screen with a field of characters for them to crawl over..SH SEE ALSOrain